TIP:  The riff runs through the entire song and you have to get it down.  It starts with a short sequence of strums beginning with (E), then hold form and strum (E7) by adding your pinky to cover note <d>, and then release back to the (E) and make a single strum emphasizing the high E (1st  string) and then move immediately to the (E) and end with an (A).  Here’s a video showing you how:   https://youtu.be/i22mHKEs78M.  This riff is played as the intro, a seque between lines, the instrumental and over the top of the outro.  Get the riff down and don’t concentrate too much where it occurs within the lyrics.  Just go with it.  The only time it breaks is the first line of the chorus.    


  
